# Repository ceiling for publishers. Host overrides may only turn an `on` value
# off. Turning a sleeve off stops publication; it does not zero targets or
# flatten exposure. Flatten through the account owner and verify venue/journal
# state before retirement. Strict KEY=value; accepted values are on/off.
LONG_SLEEVE=on
CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE=off
CONTINUOUS_PAPER_SLEEVE=off
CARRY_SLEEVE=on
# Superseded by PAPER_TARGET_MIRROR. The paper CARRY producer decided
# independently off a raced read of the demo producer's data store: over 1,633
# live cycles its funding cache matched demo's 94.2% of the time and its kline
# cache 82.4%, and on 2026-07-29 that divergence opened and closed a TLMUSDT
# position demo never asked for, for -70.73 USDT. Two producers cannot be made
# to agree by narrowing that window; one producer can. Turning this back on
# means reinstating the race, so it needs the same evidence that closed it.
CARRY_PAPER_SLEEVE=off
# Republishes the demo fleet's published targets onto the paper route, so the
# only remaining difference between the two books is execution.
PAPER_TARGET_MIRROR=on
# Real-money producers. Off in the repository, which is a hard ceiling: a host
# override can only narrow an enabled sleeve, never re-enable a disabled one,
# so turning either of these on is a committed change and not a host edit.
# Turning them on is still not sufficient -- REAL_MONEY and mainnet credentials
# are separate owner acts.
CARRY_MAINNET_SLEEVE=off
LONG_MAINNET_SLEEVE=off
